    "body": "<div align=\"center\">\n\n# ✨ Pull Request! ✨\n*Thank you for helping make the project even more snatched!* 🎀\n\n</div>\n\n---\n\n## 🍵 The Tea (Architectural Overview)\n**What is happening here?**\n* **Auto-fetch agentic RAG bug**: Disables the pre-flight auto-fetch of RAG context in the `ChatCoordinator` when running in `agentic` mode. By pre-fetching and injecting context in turn 0, agentic mode was sabotaging the model's tool use, forcing it to act like a naive RAG. Disabling it triggers true agentic RAG.\n* **Fallback to naive mode**: Implemented a dynamic routing fallback in `ChatCoordinator` to revert to `naive` mode if the request is streaming (which only supports naive) or if the active LLM provider does not support tool use.\n* **Leftovers Cleanup**: Removed legacy `query_resolver_llm` and fallback keyword arguments (`base_llm_raw` and `rag_chain`) from the constructor of `ChatCoordinator`.\n* **Tests update**: Simplified `test_header_overrides.py` by removing the test-only bypass helper `send_chat_with_autofetch_skip` since the coordinator now bypasses auto-fetch natively.\n\n**Impact Assessment:**\n- [x] 🟢 **Local Only:** No impact on other modules.\n- [ ] 🟡 **Moderate:** Affects related logic/services; requires coordinated testing.\n- [ ] 🔴 **Critical:** Changes core architecture or API contracts; high regression risk.\n\n**Linked Issues:** `Fixes #`\n\n## 💅 Type of Change\n- [x] 🐛 Bug fix (non-breaking change that fixes an issue)\n- [ ] ✨ New feature (non-breaking change that adds functionality)\n- [ ] 💥 Breaking change (fix or feature that changes existing functionality)\n- [x] 🧹 Chore / Refactor (code cleanup, dependency updates)\n- [ ] 📖 Documentation update\n\n## 🤖 Agentic Logic & Accountability\n- **Reasoning Path:** Identified that `should_auto_fetch` was running for all modes (both naive and agentic). Restricting it to naive mode and updating test cases to run natively on the default `agentic` mode restores correct tool use.\n- **Mandate Adherence:** Followed the \"Engineering & Execution Standards\" (Zero-Bypass Architecture, Precision Editing, and linting compliance) in GEMINI.md.\n- **Edge Cases Handled:** Added a dynamic fallback to naive mode in `ChatCoordinator` for cases where the provider doesn't support tools or streaming is requested, ensuring RAG context is still successfully auto-fetched in those scenarios.\n\n## ✅ Engineering Checklist\n- [x] 📦 **Dependencies:** I have run `uv sync` (and used `--no-dev` if applicable).\n- [x] 🧹 **Hygiene:** I have run `ruff-all` (or equivalent) and there are zero linting errors.\n- [x] 疤 **Syntax:** I have verified Python syntax integrity (no broken SOT files).\n- [x] 🧪 **Testing:** I have run `pytest` and provided the results below.\n\n## 📊 Test Results\n```\ntests/unit/logic/test_chat_coordinator.py .                              [  7%]\ntests/unit/logic/test_chat_coordinator_chat.py ....                      [ 35%]\ntests/integration/test_header_overrides.py ...                           [ 57%]\ntests/integration/test_rag_retrieval.py ......                           [100%]\n\n======================== 14 passed in 163.85s (0:02:43) ========================\n```\n\n<div align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Vibe-Checked-ff69b4?style=for-the-badge&logo=sparkles\" alt=\"Vibe Checked\" />\n</div>\n",
